{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-2826"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of machinery for textile, apparel and leather production"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "2826"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :textile-apparel-leather-machinery/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :mechanical-safety :electrical-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :textile-apparel-leather-machinery-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :eda :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "TexMachAdvisor ⊣ Textile, Apparel and Leather Machinery Plant
 Operations Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit
 ledger. A plant OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for textile/apparel/
 leather production-machinery manufacturing (weaving-loom/sewing-
 machine/leather-cutting-machine assembly and test lines producing
 finished weaving looms, industrial sewing machines, leather-cutting
 machines, knitting machines and fabric-cutting machines) -- not
 direct assembly/test-bench-equipment control authority and not
 machinery-safety-certification authority (e.g. CE marking under the
 EU Machinery Directive). Four ops (`:log-production-batch` /
 `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-safety-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Twelve concrete
 governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD invariants:
 propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect
 allowlist (no direct assembly/test-bench-equipment control),
 permanent equipment-actuate block, permanent safety-certification-
 authority block (this actor never self-issues a machinery safety
 certification mark), independent equipment verification/registration
 before maintenance scheduling, independent batch verification/
 registration before shipment coordination, independent shipment-
 quantity recompute against the batch's own logged production
 quantity, double-schedule guard, product-type validation, no-load-
 run-speed plausibility validation, and defect-rate plausibility
 validation. Safety-concern flagging (mechanical-safety/electrical-
 safety/CE-compliance concern) ALWAYS escalates to a human plant
 supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to
 auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
